# Mobile-first

This game is mobile-first. Every new component is designed for a 360–414 px viewport first, then progressively enhanced for larger screens.

## CSS rules

- **Use `min-width` queries**, never `max-width`. Base styles are mobile; `@media (min-width: <bp>)` adds desktop.
- Standard breakpoints: `480px`, `768px`, `1024px`, `1280px`. Reuse existing tokens where present.
- Touch targets: minimum **44×44 px** for any interactive element.
- Respect safe areas: `env(safe-area-inset-*)` for layout padding.
- Respect motion preferences: wrap heavy animations in `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`.
- Avoid `box-shadow` blur on mobile gameplay surfaces (documented FPS killer in this codebase).

## Component rules

- New components default to a single column / stacked layout.
- Inputs and controls must be operable with thumb-only interaction.
- Avoid hover-only affordances; provide explicit on-screen controls.
- Dynamic backgrounds and weather effects must offer a "reduce" path on mobile (already partially implemented; keep the discipline).

## Performance budget per component

- No layout thrashing inside `requestAnimationFrame`.
- Memoize lists and HUD sub-trees (`React.memo`, `useMemo`) when they re-render at gameplay frequency.
- Prefer `transform`/`opacity` over `top/left/width/height` for animations.
